@cmbrose I tried with `<?php echo("hello, world") ?>` but seems like that doesn't work as expected. Even `hello, world` are not printed on curl's output. 

![A screen recording showing two terminal app windows. The left one is running a php's build in web server, with the command `php -S 0.0.0.0:8888 ./info.php`. The content of `info.php` file is `<?php echo("hello, world") ?>`. The recorder runs a command `curl http://localhost:8888` on the right terminal window, the curl command keeps running without any output.](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/67255597/213162400-fc8086fb-d640-44c3-a0b8-4257c947c9be.gif)

If I appends some new line characters, `hello, world` will be printed:

![A screen recording showing two terminal app windows. The left one is running a php's build in web server, with the command `php -S 0.0.0.0:8888 ./info.php`. The content of `info.php` file is `<?php echo("hello, world\n\n\n";`. The recorder runs a command `curl http://localhost:8888` on the right terminal window, the output of the curl's output is `hello, world`, follow by 3 new lines. Then the curl command keeps running without any further output.](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/67255597/213162156-97e11785-abbc-44c0-ae69-9b77f9477091.gif)


I tried with this snippet:

```php
<?php

foreach(range(0, 100) as $i) {
    echo $i . ' ';
}
```

and this:

```php
<?php

foreach(range(0, 100) as $i) {
    echo $i . "\n";
}
```

And the result seems that if the output contains only one line, the line will not appears.
![A screen record showing two terminal windows. The left terminal window is running a php's build in web server, which runs a script that prints numbers 0 to 100, separated by a new line character. The right terminal window is running a curl command that request to that web server, the commands prints out numbers 0 to 100, then the command continues running without further outputs.](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/67255597/213164779-b136f0e3-2410-431d-9245-ec3480047993.gif)

![A screen record showing two terminal windows. The left terminal window is running a php's build in web server, which runs a script that prints numbers 0 to 100, separated by a space character. The right terminal window is running a curl command that request to that web server, the commands keeps running without any outputs.](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/67255597/213165153-4944a5dc-f7d0-4ee7-ad19-bad93c4ca6e0.gif)
